\[
M_n = \frac{8 \pi}{\hbar} \sin\left( \frac{\pi n}{N+2} \right)
\]

(in certain normalizations of the quantum KdV hierarchy).

The two-soliton state is a scattering state of two such quantum solitons, with the non-commutative phase shift preserved from the classical case.

